irely around \"send a free-text prompt, parse JSON back out of the response,\" and that whole shape doesn't apply to a typed-question API. You'd need a second scorer implementation alongside (not instead of) `LlmJudgeScorer`, mapping `correctness`/`faithfulness` (0–2) to a 3-level `Score` question and `appropriate_refusal` to a `Noul` question — which, notably, is arguably a *better* fit for a rubric like ours than hoping an LLM emits well-formed JSON.\n\nWant me to try to pin down the real Maven coordinates and merged status first, before we go further on this?"}